            <ArticleTitle>Uterine inversion as an extremely rare cause of secondary infertility: A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4274/tjod.65471</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Today, infertility takes a major place in gynecology practice. Non-puerperal uterine inversion is a rare event and usually accompanies submucous myoma, leiomyosarcoma, rhabdomyosarcoma, malignant mixed Mullerian tumour, and endometrial polyp. Herein, we report a 39-year-old woman who suffered from secondary infertility together with uterine inversion, which is an extremely rare co-existence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
